==============================================================================
H038 -- IS phidot = 0 AN ATTRACTOR, OR AN IMPOSED CONSTRAINT?  (R10)
==============================================================================

  footings: a0 = 9.3619e-11 and 1.1279e-10 m/s^2
  background: flat LCDM, H0 = 67.4 km/s/Mpc, Om = 0.315, OL = 0.685

==============================================================================
PART 1 -- THE EXACT FLRW REDUCTION OF THE SCALAR EOM
==============================================================================
  [PASS] E1 [EXACT REDUCTION] grad_mu[f'(K) d^mu phi] = 0 in homogeneous FLRW reduces
      to d_t( a^3 f'(K) phidot ) = 0, i.e. a^3 f'(K) phidot = const
         measured : divergence = -Fp(t)*Derivative(phi(t), (t, 2)) - 3*Fp(t)*Derivative(a(t), t)*Derivative(phi(t), t)/a(t) - Derivative(Fp(t), t)*Derivative(phi(t), t);  residual against -(1/a^3)d_t(a^3 f' phidot) = 0;  K(FLRW) = -Derivative(phi(t), t)**2/(2*Lambda4);  residual(K) = 0
         threshold: both symbolic residuals == 0
         This is exact, not perturbative: the scalar EOM in FLRW is a FIRST
         INTEGRAL, not a second-order equation.
  [PASS] E2 [KINEMATICS] in homogeneous FLRW  K = -phidot^2/(2 Lambda^4) <= 0
      for every real phidot, with equality iff phidot = 0
         measured : max K over |v| in [1e-8, 1e6] (v = phidot/Lambda^2) = -5.000000e-17; K at v = 0 = 0.0e+00
         threshold: K <= 0 for all v (equality only at v = 0)
         The domain K >= 0 of the homogeneous FLRW sector is ONE POINT: v = 0.
         An attractor needs a neighbourhood to attract FROM. There is none.

==============================================================================
PART 2 -- IS THE EOM REAL OFF THE FROZEN LOCUS?  (the decisive test)
==============================================================================
  [PASS] R1 [CONTINUATION] for K = -w^2, f'(K) = mu_2(i w) with
      Re = w^2(w^2+3)/(1+w^2)^2 and Im = 2w/(1+w^2)^2  (sympy exact)
         measured : residual(Re) = 0; residual(Im) = 0
         threshold: both symbolic residuals == 0
         sqrt(K) is imaginary off the frozen locus, so f'(K) is complex -- this is
         not a choice, it is what mu_2 does.
  [PASS] R2 [NO REAL DYNAMICS] Im f'(K) = 2w/(1+w^2)^2 is strictly nonzero for
      every w > 0, so the Noether current a^3 f'(K) phidot is complex
      for every nonzero phidot
         measured : min Im f' over w in [1e-6, 1e6] = 2.000000e-18; value at w = 1e-6 = 2.000000e-06
         threshold: Im f' > 0 for all w > 0 (never real)
         Consequence: there is NO real rolling homogeneous FLRW solution. The
         frozen configuration is not the endpoint of a flow -- it is the
         only real configuration.
  [PASS] R3 [low footing] a physical perturbation v = phidot/Lambda^2 = 1e-3
      gives |Im f'| / |f'| = 0.999999 (the EOM coefficient is
      not even approximately real)
         measured : Lambda^2 = 2 a0/sqrt(G) = 2.291876e-05; phidot = 2.291876e-08 SI; Im f' = 1.414212e-03, |f'| = 1.414213e-03
         threshold: |Im f'|/|f'| > 0.05
         The imaginary part is not a small correction: at small w it is the
         DOMINANT part of f' (Im ~ 2w while Re ~ 3w^2).
  [PASS] R3 [high footing] a physical perturbation v = phidot/Lambda^2 = 1e-3
      gives |Im f'| / |f'| = 0.999999 (the EOM coefficient is
      not even approximately real)
         measured : Lambda^2 = 2 a0/sqrt(G) = 2.761199e-05; phidot = 2.761199e-08 SI; Im f' = 1.414212e-03, |f'| = 1.414213e-03
         threshold: |Im f'|/|f'| > 0.05
         The imaginary part is not a small correction: at small w it is the
         DOMINANT part of f' (Im ~ 2w while Re ~ 3w^2).

